Relevant columns and their potential usage  
• SAMPLE_CONTENTS."content": search program text for import‑style statements that use parentheses, pull out quoted package names, and count them.  
• SAMPLE_CONTENTS."sample_repo_name": (optional) lets us see which repository contributed the import line.  
• SAMPLE_CONTENTS."sample_path": (optional) helps confirm file types / languages.  

Typical conditions that will be useful  
• "content" ILIKE '%import%(%'   → pick rows that actually contain a parenthesised import list.  
• REGEXP_LIKE("content", 'import[\\s\\S]*\\(')  → stricter pattern.  
• REGEXP_EXTRACT / REGEXP_REPLACE to isolate text inside the parentheses and strip double quotes.  
• SPLIT or SPLIT_TO_TABLE to break multi‑line imports into individual lines.  
• WHERE pkg_name IS NOT NULL  → ignore unmatched rows.  

Below are ten exploratory Snowflake SQL snippets (each returns ≤ 20 rows) that build from simple inspection to the final aggregation.  Adapt DATABASE / SCHEMA / TABLE names if your account aliases differ.

```sql
-- 1. Peek at raw contents to understand the data
SELECT 
    "sample_repo_name",
    "sample_path",
    LEFT("content", 500) AS "first_500_chars"
FROM GITHUB_REPOS.GITHUB_REPOS.SAMPLE_CONTENTS
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 2. Quickly find any file bodies that contain an “import (“ style construct
SELECT 
    "sample_repo_name",
    "sample_path"
FROM GITHUB_REPOS.GITHUB_REPOS.SAMPLE_CONTENTS
WHERE "content" ILIKE '%import%(%'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 3. Show only the import block (text inside the parentheses) for the first few matches
SELECT
    "sample_repo_name",
    REGEXP_SUBSTR("content", 'import[\\s\\S]*?\\)', 1, 1) AS "import_block"
FROM GITHUB_REPOS.GITHUB_REPOS.SAMPLE_CONTENTS
WHERE REGEXP_LIKE("content", 'import[\\s\\S]*\\(')
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 4. Extract import blocks, remove the surrounding word ‘import’ and parentheses
SELECT
    "sample_repo_name",
    REGEXP_REPLACE(
        REGEXP_SUBSTR("content", 'import[\\s\\S]*?\\)', 1, 1),
        '^import[\\s\\n\\r]*\\(|\\)$',
        ''
    ) AS "imports_inside"
FROM GITHUB_REPOS.GITHUB_REPOS.SAMPLE_CONTENTS
WHERE REGEXP_LIKE("content", 'import[\\s\\S]*\\(')
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 5. Split those inside‑parentheses strings into individual lines
SELECT
    t."sample_repo_name",
    TRIM(s.value)                         AS "one_import_line"
FROM GITHUB_REPOS.GITHUB_REPOS.SAMPLE_CONTENTS t,
     LATERAL SPLIT_TO_TABLE(
         REGEXP_REPLACE(
             REGEXP_SUBSTR(t."content", 'import[\\s\\S]*?\\)', 1, 1),
             '^import[\\s\\n\\r]*\\(|\\)$',
             ''
         ),
         '\n'
     ) s
WHERE REGEXP_LIKE(t."content", 'import[\\s\\S]*\\(')
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 6. Keep only lines that actually hold a quoted package path
SELECT
    TRIM(s.value) AS "raw_line"
FROM GITHUB_REPOS.GITHUB_REPOS.SAMPLE_CONTENTS t,
     LATERAL SPLIT_TO_TABLE(
         REGEXP_REPLACE(
             REGEXP_SUBSTR(t."content", 'import[\\s\\S]*?\\)', 1, 1),
             '^import[\\s\\n\\r]*\\(|\\)$',
             ''
         ),
         '\n'
     ) s
WHERE REGEXP_LIKE(t."content", 'import[\\s\\S]*\\(')
  AND s.value ILIKE '%"%"%'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 7. Extract the text that sits inside the first pair of double quotes on each line
SELECT
    REGEXP_SUBSTR(TRIM(s.value), '"([^"]+)"', 1, 1, 'e', 1) AS "pkg_name"
FROM GITHUB_REPOS.GITHUB_REPOS.SAMPLE_CONTENTS t,
     LATERAL SPLIT_TO_TABLE(
         REGEXP_REPLACE(
             REGEXP_SUBSTR(t."content", 'import[\\s\\S]*?\\)', 1, 1),
             '^import[\\s\\n\\r]*\\(|\\)$',
             ''
         ),
         '\n'
     ) s
WHERE REGEXP_LIKE(t."content", 'import[\\s\\S]*\\(')
  AND s.value ILIKE '%"%"%'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 8. Count how frequently each package string appears (preliminary, unsorted)
SELECT
    REGEXP_SUBSTR(TRIM(s.value), '"([^"]+)"', 1, 1, 'e', 1) AS "pkg_name",
    COUNT(*) AS "occurrences"
FROM GITHUB_REPOS.GITHUB_REPOS.SAMPLE_CONTENTS t,
     LATERAL SPLIT_TO_TABLE(
         REGEXP_REPLACE(
             REGEXP_SUBSTR(t."content", 'import[\\s\\S]*?\\)', 1, 1),
             '^import[\\s\\n\\r]*\\(|\\)$',
             ''
         ),
         '\n'
     ) s
WHERE REGEXP_LIKE(t."content", 'import[\\s\\S]*\\(')
  AND s.value ILIKE '%"%"%'
GROUP BY 1
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 9. Same as #8 but drop nulls and sort descending
SELECT
    pkg_name,
    COUNT(*) AS "cnt"
FROM (
    SELECT
        REGEXP_SUBSTR(TRIM(s.value), '"([^"]+)"', 1, 1, 'e', 1) AS pkg_name
    FROM GITHUB_REPOS.GITHUB_REPOS.SAMPLE_CONTENTS t,
         LATERAL SPLIT_TO_TABLE(
             REGEXP_REPLACE(
                 REGEXP_SUBSTR(t."content", 'import[\\s\\S]*?\\)', 1, 1),
                 '^import[\\s\\n\\r]*\\(|\\)$',
                 ''
             ),
             '\n'
         ) s
    WHERE REGEXP_LIKE(t."content", 'import[\\s\\S]*\\(')
      AND s.value ILIKE '%"%"%'
) sub
WHERE pkg_name IS NOT NULL
GROUP BY pkg_name
ORDER BY cnt DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 10. Final query: top‑10 most frequently used packages, quotes already stripped
SELECT
    pkg_name,
    COUNT(*) AS "cnt"
FROM (
    SELECT
        REGEXP_REPLACE(
            REGEXP_SUBSTR(TRIM(s.value), '"([^"]+)"', 1, 1, 'e', 1),
            '"', ''
        ) AS pkg_name
    FROM GITHUB_REPOS.GITHUB_REPOS.SAMPLE_CONTENTS t,
         LATERAL SPLIT_TO_TABLE(
             REGEXP_REPLACE(
                 REGEXP_SUBSTR(t."content", 'import[\\s\\S]*?\\)', 1, 1),
                 '^import[\\s\\n\\r]*\\(|\\)$',
                 ''
             ),
             '\n'
         ) s
    WHERE REGEXP_LIKE(t."content", 'import[\\s\\S]*\\(')
      AND s.value ILIKE '%"%"%'
) sub
WHERE pkg_name IS NOT NULL
GROUP BY pkg_name
ORDER BY cnt DESC
LIMIT 10;
```

Each successive query deepens the exploration from raw rows toward the final “top‑10 packages” aggregation while following the required quotation and formatting guidelines.
